              ===================  Setting up an on-premise Kubernetes cluster (Ubuntu 22.04)  ======================

. Create linux virtual machine on local or AWS Ec2 Instance (01 Master node and 02 worker nodes)
. use ssh and connect your machine.

Steps:   ( follow these stpes in each  nodes master and worker)
. after connect 
  sudo apt-get update -y
  sudo apt-get upgrade -y

Note: in Ubuntu 22.04 this may come so opt 08 option
Restarting services...
Daemons using outdated libraries
--------------------------------

  1. dbus.service                        5. systemd-logind.service
  2. networkd-dispatcher.service         6. unattended-upgrades.service
  3. packagekit.service                  7. user@1000.service
  4. polkit.service                      8. none of the above

 sudo reboot ( applying new version)

. For set hostname:
 
  sudo hostnamectl set-hostname "k8s-master.nvtienanh.local"           -- master-node
  sudo hostnamectl set-hostname "k8s-worker-node-1.nvtienanh.local"    -- worker-node-1
  sudo hostnamectl set-hostname "k8s-worker-node-2.nvtienanh.local"    -- worker-node-2

. sudo apt-get install vim            (Editor as per your requirement)
          or
  sudo apt-get install nano 

. on each node upate hostfile  for update server's ips and hostname
  sudo vim /etc/hosts

